      "id": 6,
      "claim": "Caffeine can slightly lower calcium absorption, but this effect is offset by normal dietary intake and does not lead to measurable deficits in bone growth.",
      "evidence": "Nutrition research showing a ≤5 % reduction in calcium absorption with moderate caffeine, compensated by typical diet; no impact on bone density or stature in population studies.",
